# Whether a value is a function never changes, so a test that is repeated answers as it did. Where the tested value comes together from several blocks, an edge out of the second test takes only what
# did not come from behind the other side of the first (f0); where all of it did, nothing (f2); round a loop, not what the back edge brings from behind the other side (f3).
# An object can leave its layout between two tests (f1). The way back to the first test is walked over eight blocks at most: the ninth keeps the argument among the sources of the failing edge (f4).
# RUN: valueflow-body f0 f1 f2 f3 f4
# CHECK: body f0: nodes=10 sites=0 edges=9 edgesOnceReached=0 seeds=0 statements=0
# CHECK-NEXT: n0 parameter v0
# CHECK-NEXT: n1 result
# CHECK-NEXT: n2 thrown
# CHECK-NEXT: n3 filter v1 : boolean
# CHECK-NEXT: n4 filter v3 & function
# CHECK-NEXT: n5 filter v4 - function
# CHECK-NEXT: n6 merge v5
# CHECK-NEXT: n7 merge
# CHECK-NEXT: n8 filter & function
# CHECK-NEXT: n9 filter - function
# CHECK-NEXT: edge n0 -> n3
# CHECK-NEXT: edge n3 -> n4
# CHECK-NEXT: edge n3 -> n5
# CHECK-NEXT: edge n4 -> n6
# CHECK-NEXT: edge n4 -> n8
# CHECK-NEXT: edge n5 -> n6
# CHECK-NEXT: edge n5 -> n9
# CHECK-NEXT: edge n8 -> n1
# CHECK-NEXT: edge n9 -> n1
# CHECK-NEXT: returns n0 & function as it came, the rest in n7
# CHECK-NEXT: returns n0 - function as it came, the rest in n7
# CHECK-NEXT: observed v2: n3
# CHECK-NEXT: observed v6: n6
# CHECK-NEXT: observed v1: n0
# CHECK-NEXT: body f1: nodes=9 sites=0 edges=9 edgesOnceReached=0 seeds=0 statements=0
# CHECK-NEXT: n0 parameter v0
# CHECK-NEXT: n1 result
